  --- Memory Safety Rules ---
  1. Always check malloc/calloc/realloc return (NULL = failure)
  2. Always free what you allocate
  3. Never use memory after free (use-after-free)
  4. Never free the same pointer twice (double free)
  5. Set pointer to NULL after free
  6. Allocate strlen(s)+1 for string copies
  7. Check for integer overflow: nmemb * size could overflow
  8. Use Valgrind, ASan, MSan to detect bugs

