============================================================
  SECTION 21: UB, UNSPECIFIED, IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED
============================================================

  --- Undefined Behavior (NEVER DO THESE) ---
  1. Signed overflow:     int x = INT_MAX; x++; // UB!
  2. NULL dereference:    int *p = NULL; *p = 42; // UB!
  3. Out-of-bounds:       int a[5]; a[10] = 1; // UB!
  4. Uninitialized:       int x; printf("%d", x); // UB!
  5. Modify string lit:   char *s="hi"; s[0]='H'; // UB!
  6. Double free:         free(p); free(p); // UB!
  7. Use after free:      free(p); *p = 1; // UB!
  8. Sequence point:      i = i++ + ++i; // UB!
  9. Shift overflow:      1 << 32 (if int is 32-bit) // UB!
  10. Aliasing:           float f; int *p=(int*)&f; // UB!

  Unsigned wrapping (well-defined): UINT_MAX + 1 = 0

  --- Unspecified Behavior ---
  1. f(g(), h()) ΓÇö which function runs first? unspecified
  2. a[i] = i++ ΓÇö which i is used? unspecified
  3. Struct padding bytes ΓÇö value unspecified

  --- Implementation-Defined ---
  sizeof(int)       = 4
  sizeof(long)      = 4
  char signedness   = signed
  Byte order        = little-endian
  -16 >> 2          = -4 (implementation-defined for signed)

